Pipeline artefacts are written here (raw_locations.json, normalized_locations.json,
geocoded_locations.json, enriched_pois.json, pipeline_stats.json) along with the
SQLite response caches. The contents are reproducible outputs and are git-ignored;
this file keeps the directory itself in the archive, because compose.yaml
bind-mounts it and a host directory created by the Docker daemon would be owned
by root and unwritable by the non-root container user.

Offline smoke-test runs are isolated to data/smoke/ so they can never overwrite
a real run's artefacts.
